# WEBCore

A simple WebCore HTML library that recursively scans the project directory for `.html` files and displays them as live iframe previews.

## Run

1. Install Node.js.
2. Open this folder in VS Code.
3. Open the terminal.
4. Run:

```bash
npm install
npm start
```

5. Open:

http://localhost:3000

## How the scanner works

Put HTML files anywhere inside the WEBCore folder:

```text
WEBCore/
├── index.html
├── server.js
├── previews/
│   ├── button.html
│   └── animation.html
├── components/
│   └── card.html
└── 3d/
    └── cube.html
```

All `.html` files are detected recursively. `index.html` is excluded from the preview list.

The page refreshes its library list every 5 seconds.

## Important

A browser cannot recursively inspect arbitrary local folders by itself because of browser security restrictions. `server.js` performs the folder scan and serves the files.
